| !Run for !Xriscos: the X server for the RISC OS desktop.
| Arguments are passed on to the server, e.g. -rootless or -screen 800x600x24
| (*Filer_Run doesn't pass any; use *Run <Xriscos$Dir>.!Run -rootless).
| The server's messages go to <Xriscos$Dir>.xlog.
Set Xriscos$Dir <Obey$Dir>
IconSprites <Xriscos$Dir>.!Sprites
RMEnsure UtilityModule 3.50 Error Xriscos needs RISC OS 3.5 or later
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.07 RMLoad <Xriscos$Dir>.SharedULib
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.07 Error Xriscos needs SharedUnixLibrary 1.07 or later
| The X screen and, when rootless, each window's pixels are in this slot.
WimpSlot -min 8000K -max 8000K
| The server finds its keymaps (-xkbdir) and writes its log relative to the
| current directory.
Dir <Xriscos$Dir>
Run <Xriscos$Dir>.!RunImage :0 -listen tcp -ac -xkbdir xkb %*0 2> xlog
